## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates designing an OTCA telemetry path for a real-time chat app with multi-region tenants, focusing on privacy at ingestion, data residency, and practical streaming topology.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA tenancy and data residency
- Chat-event schema (message_sent, typing events, read_receipt)
- Privacy at ingestion: redaction and hashing
- Idempotent deduplication and per-tenant rate limits
- Streaming: edge gateway, regional Kafka, Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactEvent(e){
  const copy = { ...e };
  copy.user_id_hash = hash(copy.user_id_hash);
  delete copy.personal_message;
  return copy;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify privacy guarantees across tenants during retention cycles?
- What metrics would you surface to validate QoS and latency under load?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?
